# JIT-OPTIMIZED ORDER 2, 2D IMPLEMENTATION
# ==========================================
#
# MATLAB CORRESPONDENCE:
# ----------------------
# This file corresponds to MATLAB: fastLPR/utility/core/get_lwp_estimator.m
# Specifically the symbolic Cramer's rule formula for order=2, dx=2 case
# generated by MATLAB's estimated_lwp_estimator.m
#
# The symbolic formula computes beta[1] (intercept) directly using Cramer's rule
# without matrix inversion, which is faster for the 6x6 design matrix.
#
# OPTIMIZATION NOTE:
# ------------------
# This file contains the ORDER 2, 2D symbolic Cramer's rule formula
# extracted to a top-level function to avoid R's JIT compilation overhead.
#
# ROOT CAUSE OF 15-SECOND DELAY:
# R's JIT compiler byte-compiles closures, but the massive symbolic
# formulas (tens of thousands of characters) cause a 15+ second compilation
# on the SECOND call with the same closure. By extracting to a top-level
# function, the JIT compilation happens once at package load time.
#
# @param S List of design matrix elements S[[1]] to S[[21]]
# @param T List of weighted response elements T[[1]] to T[[6]]
# @param regularization Regularization parameter (default 0)
# @return m The estimated coefficient (beta[1])
#
# @note This function is called from mfun() in lwp_estimator.R
# @seealso get_lwp_estimator
